# Findings the release scan should not block on.
#
# `.github/workflows/release-image.yml` gates every image on CRITICAL and HIGH, fixed or not,
# plus any secret found in a layer. That is strict on purpose: a base-image CVE should stop a
# release rather than ship quietly. This file is the valve, and an entry here is a decision, not
# a mute button.
#
# One CVE id per line. Write the reason above it and an expiry date, so a line that outlived its
# reason is visible as an old date rather than as a line nobody remembers adding:
#
#   # CVE-2025-0000 — in libfoo, reachable only from the CLI's --serve mode, which no image runs.
#   # Revisit 2026-12-01, or when debian ships the fix.
#   CVE-2025-0000
#
# Empty is the goal. A growing file means the base image needs bumping, not that the gate is
# wrong.

# Both of the below are inside npm's OWN vendored tree in the two executor images, which keep npm
# because Claude Code's plugin path uses it. npm 11.21.0 is the newest release on the 11 line and
# still carries them; npm 12.2.0 fixes both and breaks the build — @anthropic-ai/claude-code's
# postinstall does not place its native binary under it, and `claude plugin install` then fails
# with "claude native binary not installed". So there is no npm to upgrade to, and the alternative
# (removing npm from the executors) takes the plugin path with it.
# Neither is reachable from anything these images run: npm is a build-time tool there, and no
# runner invokes it. Revisit when @anthropic-ai/claude-code installs cleanly under npm 12.

# brace-expansion denial of service, two of them. npm 11.21.0 vendors 5.0.9; the fixes are 5.0.10
# and 5.0.11.
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278

# undici 6.28.0, denial of service via an unrequested WebSocket subprotocol. Fixed in 6.28.1.
# Nothing in these images opens a WebSocket through npm's copy.
CVE-2026-19534
